🧠 Adapter Design Pattern – Overview
🔧 Definition:
The Adapter Pattern is a structural design pattern that allows objects with incompatible interfaces to work together.

Think of it as a translator between two systems.

📦 Real-Life Analogy:
You have a USB-C port on your laptop, but your mouse uses a USB-A connector.
You use an adapter to convert USB-A → USB-C.

💡 Use Cases:
Integrating legacy code with new APIs.

Allowing two incompatible classes to work together.

Reusing existing code without modifying it.